  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Kalia Sahu @ Musa vs State Of Orissa .... Opposite Party on 26 October, 2022 Author: V. Narasingh Bench: V. Narasingh In The High Court Of Orissa At Cuttack Blapl No. 9738 of 2022 Kalia Sahu @ Musa .... Petitioner Mr. J. Sahoo, Advocate -versus- State of Orissa .... Opposite Party Mr. A. Pradhan, Asc Coram: Justice V. Narasingh",
    "facts": "3. The petitioner is an accused in connection with G.R. Case No.1498 of 2022, pending in the file of the learned S.D.J.M., Berhampur, Ganjam, arising out of Berhampur Town P.S. Case No.175 of 2022, for commission of offences under Sections 420/272/273/34 of IPC read with Section 52(a)(i)/55 of Odisha Excise Act & Section 59 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006.",
    "arguments": "5. It is submitted by the learned counsel for the petitioner that since charge-sheet has already been filed on 02.08.2022, further continuance of the petitioner in custody is unwarranted. 6. Learned counsel for the State opposes the prayer for bail inter alia on the ground that the natures of allegations are serious and is a threat to public health.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "5. It is submitted by the learned counsel for the petitioner that since charge-sheet has already been filed on 02.08.2022, further continuance of the petitioner in custody is unwarranted.",
    "respondent_arguments": "6. Learned counsel for the State opposes the prayer for bail inter alia on the ground that the natures of allegations are serious and is a threat to public health.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
